{"name":"Bordeaux","hex":"#7b002c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bordeaux","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The capital city of Gironde department, France; the capital city of the region of Nouvelle-Aquitaine.","A surname from French."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wine coming from that area.","Ellipsis of Bordeaux mixture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bordeaux"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bordeaux","blocks":[{"text":"Bordeaux is a city on the river Garonne in the Gironde department, southwestern France. A port city, it is the capital of the Nouvelle-Aquitaine region, as well as the prefecture of the Gironde department. Its inhabitants are called \"Bordelais\" (masculine) or \"Bordelaises\" (feminine). The term \"Bordelais\" may also refer to the city and its surrounding region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bordeaux_Place_de_la_Bourse_de_nuit.jpg/330px-Bordeaux_Place_de_la_Bourse_de_nuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bordeaux","wikidata":"Q1479"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red","wikidata":"Q3014419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Bordeaux_Cath%C3%A9drale_Saint-Andr%C3%A9_Tour_Pey-Berland_04.jpg/500px-Bordeaux_Cath%C3%A9drale_Saint-Andr%C3%A9_Tour_Pey-Berland_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Bordeaux_Cath%C3%A9drale_Saint-Andr%C3%A9_Tour_Pey-Be